WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.640
Ask a group of unrelated people how&nbsp;
all life in the universe was created,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.000
and they would each probably&nbsp;
give you a different answer.&nbsp;

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Ask someone with a scientific background and&nbsp;
they’ll tell you the universe was birthed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.960
after the Big Bang, and that life gradually&nbsp;
evolved on Earth over millions of years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:22.160
Or, if you were to ask someone of the Christian&nbsp;
faith, they might tell you that, God created the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:28.800
entire universe in six days - every planet, star,&nbsp;
even giving life to every single creature - then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.000
took Sunday off. Every belief system since&nbsp;
the dawn of humanity, whether monotheistic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.760
pantheistic, or even atheistic, have had&nbsp;
their own creation stories and myths.&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.880
And then there’s the answer that a member of&nbsp;
The Church of The Broken God would give you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.000
and trust us, it’s far more complicated.
Just in case you’ve never heard them mentioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.560
before, The Church of The Broken God is an&nbsp;
anomalous religious organization and Group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:59.520
of Interest. The SCP Foundation has actually had&nbsp;
a number of encounters with the Church over the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.800
years, and we’ll get to why that is in a moment.&nbsp;
Members of the Church share in the belief that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:11.040
life - specifically biological, flesh-based life&nbsp;
like that of human beings - is inherently wrong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.320
a direct product of evil. Their religion&nbsp;
focuses on the worship of mechanization,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.560
which is the process of making something,&nbsp;
or someone, more mechanical in nature.&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.840
So, what do members of the Church&nbsp;
believe created life in the universe?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.120
Well, according to their beliefs, in the&nbsp;
beginning, there were two ancient and powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.000
beings. It was these gods, named Yaldabaoth&nbsp;
and Mekhane, who created humanity together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.600
Yaldabaoth was the god of flesh and animal&nbsp;
instinct, granting humans bodies while Mekhane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:48.000
the god of machine and intellect, blessed man with&nbsp;
the power of free thought. As humankind developed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:54.320
its civilizations began building machines. This&nbsp;
enraged Yaldabaoth, seeing that the humans were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:00.000
ignoring the instincts she had bestowed upon&nbsp;
them. As a result, she swore to destroy all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.240
creations of man, seeking to revert them back to&nbsp;
the animalistic state she had intended for them.&nbsp;

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.360
According to the Church’s legend, Mekhane&nbsp;
acted as humanity’s savior, and intervened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:17.040
to stop Yaldabaoth. The god of machines shattered&nbsp;
himself, transforming his metal body into a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.880
of pieces to form a cage for his fellow god.&nbsp;
These fragments of Mekhane’s body rained down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:28.800
on planet Earth, scattered and lost. The Church&nbsp;
of the Broken God believes it is their duty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:35.200
their only true purpose, to recover those&nbsp;
pieces. As such, the Church is devoted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:41.040
the worship of Mekhane, their broken god that&nbsp;
lies in fragments scattered across the world.&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:45.360
Often using anomalous technology, members&nbsp;
of the Church of The Broken God intend to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.800
uncover or steal these various components. The&nbsp;
Church’s ultimate goal is to bring the correct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.640
pieces together and eventually restore Mekhane’s&nbsp;
form. It is their hope that he will guide them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.600
intellectual enlightenment, and bless them&nbsp;
with new, mechanical forms so that they can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:07.360
discard their mortal bodies of flesh and blood,&nbsp;
and ascend to a fully mechanized way of life.&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:12.240
The one problem is there could potentially&nbsp;
be hundreds of pieces required in order to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.640
rebuild Mekhane. He cannot lead the Church&nbsp;
to glory and defeat Yaldabaoth once and for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:22.400
all with parts still missing. A number of these&nbsp;
pieces have already surfaced as cataloged SCPs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.400
that the Foundation is either aware of, or&nbsp;
has in containment. Among them are SCP-882&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:36.480
or ‘His Broken Heart’ to the Church, SCP-271,&nbsp;
His Broken Gift, SCP-813, His Broken Eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:44.560
SCP-1139, His Broken Tongue, SCP-635, His&nbsp;
Broken Mind, and finally His Broken Blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:54.160
which refers to SCP-217. And then there’s&nbsp;
SCP-3179, sometimes referred to as The Seed.&nbsp;

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.280
In 1909, a meteor shower rained over&nbsp;
Dellinton. a tiny village in England. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:05.600
something else fell with the meteors, something&nbsp;
otherworldly. It was made out of liquid metal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:10.720
its form constantly shifting and shimmering,&nbsp;
never staying at the same mass or held in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:16.480
same shape for long. The object, whatever it was,&nbsp;
quickly fell into the possession of a group known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:21.520
as the Cogwork Orthodoxy. You see, within the&nbsp;
religion of the Church of the Broken God there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:28.080
exists a number of splinter factions that,&nbsp;
ironically, broke away from the main Church.&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.880
One such group, referred to as the Cogwork&nbsp;
Orthodox Church, augment their own bodies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:38.320
through mechanical implants. However, we aren’t&nbsp;
talking microchips, the Cogwork Orthodox Church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:42.800
will only use technology from the late&nbsp;
Industrial Revolution, as they think it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:48.480
is more fitting of their god, Mekhane.
So, what does this object, SCP-3179,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:52.800
have to do with all these tales of&nbsp;
mechanical churches and broken gods?&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:59.440
SCP-3179 is capable of extending its mass,&nbsp;
forming long, rod-like metal structures that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:04.720
protrude from its central mass. These rods&nbsp;
are then used to create smaller entities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:12.000
referred to as SCP-3179-1. These entities&nbsp;
might lack the ability to expand or change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:18.800
shape the same way that SCP-3179 can, but they&nbsp;
are specialized for a wide range of functions.&nbsp;

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:26.560
The SCP-3179-1 creations are usually designed&nbsp;
to help free SCP-3179 from its containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:30.480
and will obey this purpose without&nbsp;
exception, yet somehow they do not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.880
appear capable of communicating with the&nbsp;
main body that they were created from.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:41.120
While SCP-3179 remains as a constant mass of&nbsp;
liquid metal, the entities it creates are able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:48.880
to simulate an exterior organic appearance.&nbsp;
In other words, they look like they are alive.&nbsp;

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:54.320
Still struggling to figure out why the Cogwork&nbsp;
Orthodoxy and Church of the Broken God would be so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.960
interested in this thing? Well, maybe&nbsp;
this will answer that burning question.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:06.240
Warranty Silas, One of the members of the Cogwork&nbsp;
Orthodoxy that recovered SCP-3179, thought the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:11.360
metallic object was The Seed of Mekhane.&nbsp;
According to the beliefs of the Church,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.360
this liquid metal entity would one day expand&nbsp;
to form the offspring of their Broken God.&nbsp;

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:22.560
Perhaps hoping to protect the future child&nbsp;
of their faith’s deity, the Cogwork Orthodoxy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:30.800
constructed a containment bunker around SCP-3179&nbsp;
in 1917. At first, this sturdy container seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.560
to have done its job, possibly having even been&nbsp;
made using anomalous methods or properties to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:43.920
SCP-3179 in place. For over a hundred years,&nbsp;
it successfully held the entity and restricted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:49.520
its ability to grow. However, the unit has since&nbsp;
been damaged by multiple attempts by the entity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.800
to breach its containment, and will likely&nbsp;
fail completely within the next five years.&nbsp;

00:06:54.800 --> 00:07:02.880
You see, SCP-3179 isn’t just alive, but sentient.&nbsp;
The liquid metal entity has displayed an extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:08.560
high level of intelligence, although not through&nbsp;
direct communication. It shows its intelligence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:14.000
through its evolving tactics, changing the&nbsp;
shape of its mass or creating more instances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:22.160
of SCP-3179-1 to aid in its escape. In fact, the&nbsp;
so-called Seed of Mekhane is so vastly intelligent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:27.600
in its strategies and relentless in its goal&nbsp;
to breach its containment, that in 2016 most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:33.200
of the containment unit built around it had been&nbsp;
destroyed. The Cogwork Orthodoxy had no choice but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:41.200
to directly contact the SCP Foundation, and appeal&nbsp;
to them to take over the containment of SCP-3179.&nbsp;

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:47.200
Even after this exchange, the Foundation still had&nbsp;
significant trouble keeping the entity contained.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:53.200
They couldn’t transport it, instead assigning a&nbsp;
Mobile Task Force, Zeta 10, codenamed Death Metal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:08:00.960
to monitor SCP-3179’s growth. If a section of its&nbsp;
body expanded too far beyond an acceptable level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:06.880
these personnel had to step in and&nbsp;
sever it from the main body of SCP-3179.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:11.280
Any part sliced, severed, or otherwise&nbsp;
removed from the liquid metal mass still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:16.800
continues to grow for several hours after its&nbsp;
removal. However, this growth eventually stops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:22.080
and these pieces are left inert and lifeless.
For example, on one occasion in late December&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:30.320
of 2016, SCP-3179 grew a number of metal supports&nbsp;
from its main body, not unlike multiple pairs of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:35.520
legs. Before the entity could use these new&nbsp;
appendages to pull itself free and escape its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.280
containment, members of MTF Death Metal stepped&nbsp;
in and severed them before they could fully grow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:48.000
A few weeks later in January of 2017,&nbsp;
SCP-3179 tried a similar strategy:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.120
growing structures resembling propellers on&nbsp;
the top of its body and attempting to attain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.120 --> 00:09:00.000
flight. Once again, Death Metal did what&nbsp;
they do best and clipped SCP-3179’s wings.&nbsp;

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:07.200
It later produced instances of SCP-3179-1 in the&nbsp;
form of numerous flying drones, that it tried to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:13.440
use to fly away from the containment zone. MTF&nbsp;
Zeta 10 was able to shoot these entities down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:19.840
forcing SCP-3179 to once again alter its tactics.&nbsp;
Next, it produced a number of sound-emitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:25.280
structures from its central mass and used them&nbsp;
to mimic the voices of a number of MTF Zeta 10&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:29.360
members. The metallic creature attempted&nbsp;
to plead with the Foundation’s operatives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:34.880
in the voices of their colleagues, claiming that&nbsp;
they had become trapped inside the liquid metal.&nbsp;

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:42.160
After no result, a day later SCP-3179 began using&nbsp;
the same structures to emit screams of the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:50.240
MTF Zeta 10 troops. This time, the voices claimed&nbsp;
that SCP-3179 was killing them, and begged to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:55.440
set free. Once again, the Foundation’s personnel&nbsp;
remained at their posts, though this breach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.440 --> 00:10:02.480
attempt apparently added a lot more job stress to&nbsp;
the role. SCP-3179 even, on multiple occasions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:09.920
produced instances of SCP-3179-1 that were&nbsp;
identical to existing MTF Zeta 10 members,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.720
trying to convince the others that the entity&nbsp;
should be released from its containment zone.&nbsp;

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:21.600
At one point it was even able to use tiny&nbsp;
SCP-3179-1s to replace the internal organs of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:28.160
one of the MTF Zeta 10 members in his sleep with&nbsp;
entirely mechanical components. On the outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:33.760
the man looked to be human, his eyes,&nbsp;
skin, and tongue all organic. But inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:39.440
he had been made a puppet of SCP-3179 and&nbsp;
sent off to sabotage a number of systems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:44.320
involved in the entity’s containment. Luckily,&nbsp;
the Foundation’s forces were able to stop this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:51.520
new instance of SCP-3179-1 and terminated him.
Of course, this all begs the question,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:58.640
why would the Cogwork Orthodoxy hand SCP-3179&nbsp;
over to the Foundation? If the Seed of Mekhane was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:04.960
so sacred to them, so important to their belief&nbsp;
system, then why give it to another organization?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:08.640
You could argue that the Cogwork&nbsp;
Orthodoxy were admitting that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:13.040
weren’t as well equipped as the Foundation&nbsp;
are when it comes to containing anomalies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:17.920
or that they’d rather the future offspring&nbsp;
of Mekhane was best kept as safe as possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:24.640
But that is if you even believe that SCP-3179&nbsp;
really is The Seed of Mekhane. While growing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:29.120
in its containment, the entity showed to be&nbsp;
considerably hostile towards the members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:34.160
the Church that curated it. It even caused&nbsp;
a number of casualties, killing many that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:39.200
wanted to protect it on behalf of Mekhane.
Additionally, the metallic mass wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.440
change its state whenever they would read&nbsp;
scripture relating to the Broken God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:48.720
in fact, it showed little reaction at all to any&nbsp;
displays of faith from the Cogwork Orthodoxy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:55.840
Surely Mekhane’s own offspring wouldn’t have&nbsp;
behaved in such a way. Unless, of course, SCP-3179&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:02.640
wasn’t the Seed of Mekhane at all. What if this&nbsp;
entity was an imposter, oblivious of the beliefs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:07.760
of the Church of The Broken God? And given&nbsp;
how intelligent it had shown itself to be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:14.000
surely SCP-3179 would know to take advantage of&nbsp;
the faith of those that had tried to procure it.&nbsp;

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:20.960
On the second of June 2017, SCP-3179 produced&nbsp;
a number of metal tablets from itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:25.600
and dispersed them throughout the containment&nbsp;
area surrounding it. Each tablet had the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:33.440
inscription written on it: “Humans must obey the&nbsp;
ruling of gods. The Mekhane is a god. The Mekhane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:42.320
is a powerful entity of steel and industry. I am a&nbsp;
powerful entity of steel and industry. Therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:52.320
I am Mekhane. Therefore, I am a god.&nbsp;
Therefore, you will release me.”&nbsp;

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:58.320
It is entirely possible that SCP-3179&nbsp;
was indeed a part of Mekhane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:04.080
the ancient, Broken God and deity to the Church&nbsp;
and the Cogwork Orthodoxy. But then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:09.840
this entity showed intelligence and adaptability,&nbsp;
as well as hostility towards the human beings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:15.600
around it. Perhaps this so-called Seed of Mekhane&nbsp;
was nothing more than a false prophet, trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:22.000
to use the faith of the Church to ensure its own&nbsp;
escape. It doesn’t get much craftier than that...&nbsp;

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:27.600
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Broken God -&nbsp;
Ouroboros Cycle” and “What Actually Happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.600 --> 00:13:34.720
to Major Alexei Belitrov? SCP-2273 - Tale” for&nbsp;
more lore from the Church of the Broken God!

